      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T03:36:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I know, Android devices and many minimal test images don\u0027t have `/bin/busybox`, so there the test would stop at `not ok 1` without testing `mmap2()` at all.\n\nWould you mind creating the backing file in the test instead, e.g. a temporary file or a `memfd_create()` file with a different byte pattern in each 4KB block? That would also make a mapping of the wrong slice fail reliably, rather than depending on what busybox happens to contain at those offsets.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "2938864382977e3e9e2014af7c0ce70be2f99e70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0f683fe_f5b3f9f1",
        "filename": "tools/testing/selftests/arm64/abi/aarch32-mmap2-ppps.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
