        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T03:36:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this test only passes when it is already running as a 4KB process. AArch32 tasks don\u0027t get 4KB pages by default: `mm_init_pte_shift()` only picks them for `ADDR_PAGE_SIZE_4KB` or `p3s_4k\u003d`, and nothing here sets either.\n\nAs far as I can see, when `run_kselftest.sh` runs it directly on a 16KB kernel (P3S or not), `aarch32_mmap2()` rejects `off_4k` 1 to 3 with `-EINVAL`, so tests 2-4 report `not ok`.\n\nCould the test set `ADDR_PAGE_SIZE_4KB` and re-exec itself through `/proc/self/exe`, like `ppps_compat_main()` that aosp/4367942 adds to `tools/testing/selftests/kselftest_ppps.h`, and skip if `AT_PAGESZ` still isn\u0027t 4096 after that?\n\nBuilding it with nolibc, like `tpidr2` in this Makefile, would give you `getauxval()`, `execve()` and an `mmap()` that already goes through `__NR_mmap2` with a 4KB offset on ARM, so most of the hand-written syscall wrappers could go.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "2938864382977e3e9e2014af7c0ce70be2f99e70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
